hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1414","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, Al-Masoudi and Yahya told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, so I said to Abdullah bin Abi Bakr: A hadith narrated to us by Yahya and Al-Masoudi, on the authority of your father, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, who said: I heard it from Abbad bin Tamim, who narrated My father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “went to the prayer place and drew water, then turned his cloak over and prayed two rak’ahs.” Al-Masoudi said, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, I said to him: Tell us: Did He make the top of it the bottom of it, or the bottom of it the top of it, or how did He make it? He said: No, rather he made the right the left and the left the right."
